Release/acquire over normal coherent CPU memory proves only relations provided by that language/platform mapping. DMA may observe a different coherence domain; descriptor cache lines may need clean operations; the doorbell may be device memory requiring an I/O barrier; ownership can race with device reads; completion interrupts and buffer reuse need reciprocal ordering. IOMMU, bus, firmware, and power-failure behavior also matter.

